{"id":"board-fast-track","title":"Passed without a committee hearing, or within two weeks","question":"Which files skipped the usual committee hearing or were voted within two weeks of introduction, and do files approved after the fact move faster?","finding":"Of 2,326 timed files, 29 show no committee hearing before the final vote and 36 were voted within 14 days of introduction; 107 more were sent from committee to the full Board “as a committee report”, a wording in the Board’s own history. 17 of the 49 files listed are grants the City accepts, not payments to anyone. Speed does not track approval after the fact: among contract, grant, lease and loan files, those approved after the work or term had begun took a typical 42 days (189 files) against 35 for the rest (1,309 files), and ran +7.1 days against like files compared with +2.0. 7% of the fast-tracked contract-type files were approved after the fact, against 13% of all such files.","how":"From the action history of each timed file: a committee hearing is any dated action by a body with \"Committee\" in its name; \"without committee reference\" and \"committee report\" are the Board’s own wordings in that history. A file is listed when it shows no committee hearing or reached its final vote within 14 days. \"Approved after the fact\" is the Board-file table’s flag for a title that approves an agreement retroactively. Listed quickest first. A party is shown only when it is an organization or a public body; parties to legal settlements are not shown.","limits":"Adoption without committee reference and the committee report are the Board’s own recorded procedures, printed in each file’s public history. A missing committee line can also be a gap in the published history. Late approval and fast approval are different things: a file approved after the fact was late before it was introduced, which this measure does not see. What would settle a row: the file’s own history page and the minutes of the meeting that adopted it. Amounts, parties and dates taken from Board file titles are read by machine: in a hand check of 50 titles, 11 had at least one field read wrongly (4 after later fixes).","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"file","t":"Board file","type":"link"},{"k":"introduced","t":"Introduced","type":"date"},{"k":"days","t":"Days to the final vote","type":"days"},{"k":"kind","t":"Kind","type":"text"},{"k":"department","t":"Department","type":"text"},{"k":"with","t":"With","type":"org"},{"k":"amount","t":"Amount in the title","type":"usd"},{"k":"why","t":"Why it is listed","type":"text"},{"k":"afterTheFact","t":"Approved after the fact","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"file":{"t":"File 250035","u":"https://sfgov.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=7089521&GUID=C9804949-0FF1-49BA-8F56-B819DA5A9053"},"introduced":"2025-01-08","days":6,"kind":"grant the City accepts","department":"Public Works","amount":20000000,"why":"no committee hearing on record; final vote within two weeks","afterTheFact":"","with":"Rebuilding American Infrastructure with Sustainability and Equity (RAISE) Program of the United States Department of Transportation","withKey":null},{"file":{"t":"File 250025","u":"https://sfgov.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=7089515&GUID=47E585FD-DBEF-4CFD-AAB1-7C30C92A1EE2"},"introduced":"2025-01-08","days":6,"kind":"grant the City accepts","department":"Environment","amount":19994217,"why":"no committee hearing on record; final vote within two weeks","afterTheFact":"yes"},{"file":{"t":"File 250030","u":"https://sfgov.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=7089518&GUID=B429E321-498B-4EEA-B213-B5F136200935"},"introduced":"2025-01-08","days":6,"kind":"grant the City accepts","department":"Environment","amount":14996876,"why":"no committee hearing on record; final vote within two weeks","afterTheFact":"","with":"United States Department of Transportation","withKey":null},{"file":{"t":"File 250022","u":"https://sfgov.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=7089513&GUID=ECFD0D33-B8